.TH NIXOS 1 "" "NixOS Flake Helper" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
nixos \- unified wrapper for managing the NixOS flake

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nixos
.RI [ command ] " [args]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B nixos
command is a user-facing wrapper for managing the NixOS flake.
It provides a curated set of high-level commands for carrying out
routine tasks.

When invoked without a command,
.B nixos
displays the flake directory tree with files listed first.

If an unrecognized command is provided, it is dispatched verbatim
inside the flake directory
.RB ( $NIXOS_DIR ),
allowing arbitrary commands to be run relative to the flake.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B test
Activate the new configuration without creating a boot entry.
Changes are lost on reboot.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B switch
Activate the new configuration and create a boot entry,
also format the flake.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B commit
Activate the new configuration, create a boot entry, format the flake,
fix file permissions, and create a Git commit.
.br
Roles: laptop only

.TP
.B update " [inputs...]"
Update flake inputs in
.BR flake.lock .
If no inputs are specified, all inputs are updated.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B format
Format all Nix files in the flake using
.BR nixfmt .
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B perms
Fix file ownership and permissions in the flake.
All files are set to mode 600, directories to 700, and scripts under
.B $NIXOS_DIR/scripts/
to 700.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B purge
Delete all non-current system generations.
This is a destructive operation.
Equivalent to:
.br
.B sudo nix-collect-garbage --delete-old
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B repair
Verify and repair the Nix store.
Equivalent to:
.br
.B sudo nix-store --verify --check-contents --repair
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B edit " <vars|sops>"
Edit variables or secrets associated with the flake.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B serverpush " <path>"
Push the local flake to
.BR server:<path> .
.br
Roles: laptop only

.TP
.B help
Display a brief usage summary and exit.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.SH DISPATCH BEHAVIOR
If a command does not match one of the built-in subcommands,
.B nixos
executes it directly inside
.BR $NIXOS_DIR .

This allows convenient interaction with the flake repository, such as:

.nf
nixos git status
nixos cat flake.nix | wl-copy
nixos vi modules/common/firewall.nix
.fi

.SH LOCKING
To prevent concurrent execution,
.B nixos
creates a lockfile at
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nixos-script.lock
for the following commands:
test, switch, commit, update, purge, format, perms, and init.

.SH NOTES
All commands are intended to be run through the
.B nixos
wrapper and not executed directly.
The wrapper automatically escalates privileges using
.B sudo
when required.

Command execution time is reported on completion.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B $NIXOS_DIR/scripts/
Implementation of all subcommands.

.TP
.B $NIXOS_DIR/docs/scripts.md
Full documentation.

